    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "19. At-a-Glance Summary"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Genders: Masculine · Feminine · Neuter"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Cases: Nominative · Accusative · Genitive (marked on articles/determiners)"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Tenses: Present · Present Progressive · Imperfect · Plusquamperfect · Plusquamimperfect · Future I · Future II"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Voices: Active · Passive ( wærre/wirde + pp) · Middle/Neutral ( sik particle or -st suffix)"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Moods: Indicative · Conditional I & II ( wulde ) · Imperative"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Word order: SVO main clause · V2 inversion · SOV subordinate clause · Negation nicht / ikke after the finite verb"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Infinitive: -e suffix · Past participle: ge- prefix + stem + -t/-d (weak) or -en (strong)"
    },
    {
      "type": "h3",
      "text": "Learning Progression"
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Pronunciation drills (week 1) — get comfortable with the vowel system, especially æ, ø, å, ü ."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Pronouns + present tense + SVO statements (weeks 1–2)."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Questions, negation, and simple past (weeks 2–3)."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Articles, cases, and noun gender (weeks 3–4)."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Compound tenses (perfect, pluperfect, futures) (weeks 4–6)."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Voice (passive, mediopassive) and conditional (weeks 6–8)."
    },
    {
      "type": "li",
      "text": "Free reading: translate short Norwegian or German news headlines using only Intergermanic forms — a fast way to test mutual intelligibility in both directions."
